_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/5646","id":653656462,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY1MzY1NjQ2Mg==","user":{"login":"laramiel","id":9807819,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4MDc4MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9807819?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/laramiel","html_url":"https://github.com/laramiel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/laramiel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/laramiel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/laramiel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/laramiel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/laramiel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/laramiel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/laramiel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/laramiel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/laramiel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-07-03T19:23:46Z","updated_at":"2020-07-03T19:23:46Z","body":"I spent some time looking at this, but didn't find a codepath that leads to this state.\r\n\r\nSo instead I reconsidered where I had added the connclose() call:\r\n\r\ncurl signals that data is available to the nghttp2 protocol library by calling nghttp2_session_mem_recv(). Instead of checking at http_done, instead we can check whether the server has requested a connection be closed after the mem_recv() call, since that's the only place where the state changes.\r\n\r\nSo I reviewed all the mem_recv() calls. It turns out that there were 3 codepaths, all similar, but also different.\r\nI consolidated them to use the existing h2_process_pending_input() method.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/653656462/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"